Simple Definition

Client Applications

Applications or users that send SQL queries to PostgreSQL.

Connection

A communication channel between the client and PostgreSQL.

Postmaster

The main PostgreSQL process that starts the server, accepts client connections, and creates backend processes.

Backend Process

A dedicated process that executes SQL queries for one client connection.

Shared Memory

A common area in RAM shared by all backend processes to improve performance and coordination.

Shared Buffers

The main cache that stores frequently accessed table and index pages in memory.

WAL Buffers

Temporary memory that stores change (WAL) records before they are written to WAL files on disk.

CLOG (pg_xact)

Stores the commit status of transactions (Committed, Aborted, or In Progress).

Lock Table

Keeps track of locks held by transactions to prevent conflicting operations.

Background Workers

Internal PostgreSQL processes that perform maintenance and system tasks automatically.

BGWriter

Writes modified (dirty) pages from Shared Buffers to data files gradually in the background.

WAL Writer

Writes WAL records from WAL Buffers to WAL files on disk.

Checkpointer

Periodically writes dirty pages to disk and creates checkpoints for faster crash recovery.

Autovacuum

Automatically removes dead rows and updates table statistics to maintain performance.

Statistics Collector

Collects database usage statistics that help the query planner choose efficient execution plans.

Archiver

Copies completed WAL files to an archive location for backup and recovery.

Logical Replication Worker

Sends or applies data changes to another PostgreSQL server using logical replication.

Autovacuum Launcher

Monitors databases and starts Autovacuum workers when needed.

Data Files

Files on disk that store the actual database tables, indexes, and other objects.

WAL Files (pg_wal)

Files that record every database change before it is written to the data files.

Archive

Long-term storage of WAL files used for backup and Point-in-Time Recovery (PITR).

Logs

Files that record PostgreSQL events such as startup, shutdown, errors, and connections.

